NAME
       futex - fast userspace lock

SYNOPSIS
       int futex_wait(int *addr, int expected);
       int futex_wake(int *addr, int count);

DESCRIPTION
       The kernel half of a userspace lock. futex_wait sleeps only if
       the word at ADDR still equals EXPECTED, which closes the race
       between testing the lock and going to sleep. futex_wake wakes up
       to COUNT waiters.

       The uncontended path stays entirely in userspace and costs no
       syscall; the kernel is only involved when a thread actually has
       to wait.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       semget(2), poll(2)
